'''''Meterchen''''' is an [[Extinction|extinct]] [[Monotypic taxon|monotypic genus]] of [[Anserinae|anserine]] [[Anatidae|anatid]] that lived during the [[Burdigalian]] [[Stage (stratigraphy)|stage]] of the [[Miocene]] [[Geologic time scale|epoch]].

== Etymology ==
The [[Generic name (biology)|generic name]] ''Meterchen'' means 'mother goose' in [[Ancient Greek]], and the [[Binomial nomenclature|specific epithet]] ''luti'' means 'of the mud' in [[Latin]]. The binomen therefore references the [[Mother Goose]] [[nursery rhyme]] where a mother goose rises up out of the mud.<ref>{{Cite journal |last1=Tennyson |first1=Alan J. D. |last2=Steell |first2=Elizabeth M. |last3=Lubbe |first3=Pascale |last4=Adams |first4=Amy L. |last5=Greer |first5=Liam |last6=Brown |first6=Alex H. |last7=Wilson |first7=Laura J. E. |last8=Campbell |first8=Timothy C. |last9=Dale |first9=Tobia C. |last10=Rawlence |first10=Nicolas J. |date=17 February 2026 |title=A review of fossil goose (Aves: Anserinae) records from the Miocene St Bathans deposits, New Zealand, with the description of a new species |url=https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/08912963.2025.2601236#d1e2353 |journal=[[Historical Biology]] |language=en |pages=1–21 |doi=10.1080/08912963.2025.2601236 |issn=0891-2963 |access-date=30 March 2026 |via=Taylor and Francis Online|url-access=subscription }}</ref>

